{
  // Cloudflare Worker fronting the site root. See index.js for what it does and
  // docs/runbooks/publishing.md for how it is deployed.
  //
  // The route is the root path ONLY, not claustodian.dev/*. Everything under
  // /data is served straight from Pages, so a Worker fault cannot take the
  // dataset offline — the blast radius is one HTML page.
  //
  // KNOWN LIMIT, measured not assumed: this pattern matches the bare root and
  // NOT https://claustodian.dev/?anything. Cloudflare matches a route against
  // the whole URL, query string included, and refuses a `?` inside a pattern
  // (API error 10022), so there is no pattern that means "root with any query".
  // Verified 8/8 alternating requests: bare root negotiates, ?cb=… does not.
  //
  // Accepted deliberately, and it costs less than it sounds: nothing here ever
  // produces such a URL. The site uses no query parameters at all — no
  // URLSearchParams, no location.search, no pushState in site/index.html or
  // site/review/index.html; search and pagination are in-memory, so no link the
  // site emits carries a query. A query string on / only arrives from outside:
  // a sharer's tracking parameters, a crawler, or a cache-busting probe. Each of
  // those gets HTML, which is the right default anyway.
  //
  // Covering it means routing claustodian.dev/* and guarding on pathname inside
  // the Worker, which puts all ~800 data files behind it. Keeping the dataset
  // out of the Worker's blast radius is worth more than negotiating a request
  // shape nothing in this repo generates, and the uncovered case degrades to
  // HTML rather than erroring.
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "claustodian-site",
  "main": "index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-09",
  "routes": [
    {
      "pattern": "claustodian.dev/",
      "zone_name": "claustodian.dev",
    },
    {
      // The MCP endpoint. Exact path, same reasoning as the root: an MCP client
      // POSTs to /mcp with no query string, so the query-string limit above
      // does not bite here.
      "pattern": "claustodian.dev/mcp",
      "zone_name": "claustodian.dev",
    },
  ],
  // No public workers.dev entry point; the route is the only way in.
  "workers_dev": false,
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true,
  },
}
